// ==========================================================================
// data/planes/cessna172/tornado.jsonc for the Cessna 172 source analysis, generated -- do not hand-edit.
//
// 1. SOLVER, MESH, FLIGHT CONDITION
//    Solver: Tornado, via the sibling package aid.tornado (imported from /home/valentin/Projects/FlightSimulation/USAF_DATCOM/AircraftIntuitiveDesign/Python/src).
//    Mesh: 10 chordwise x 5 spanwise (the AID batch default).  NP[0],
//    the AR 33.3, S 3 ft^2 panel, is KEPT in the lattice and carries
//    9.6% of the aircraft's CL at the trim alpha.
//    Flight condition from the source AERO: Mach 0.03, altitude 0.0 ft, betha 0.0 rad,
//    evaluated at alpha = 4 deg (the middle of AERO.ALSCHD), V = 10.2073 m/s, rho = 1.225056 kg/m^3.
//
// 2. THE SOURCE PLANFORM IS A CESSNA 172 AT ROUGHLY 1/3 LINEAR SCALE
//    span 12 ft against a real 36.1 ft, chord 2 ft against 4.89 ft, area 24 ft^2
//    against 174 ft^2.  Wing loading is therefore 6.70 lbf/ft^2 where a real C172 is
//    13.2.  Nothing in this file may be compared with a full-scale figure.
//
// 3. MASS
//    mass_kg = 72.574 is the source file's own AERO.WT = 5 slugs (5 x 32 ft/s^2 = 160.0 lbf,
//    160.0 / 2.2046226 = 72.574 kg).  This is NOT a geometrically similar 1/3 scale C172,
//    which would weigh about 53.5 kg, so no scaling of a published full-scale number is self-
//    consistent and none was attempted.  ixx, iyy, izz come from radius-of-gyration rules on THIS
//    mass and THIS span (see below); ixz = 0 and he = 0.
//
// 4. UNIT CONVERSIONS APPLIED, AND THE ONES NOT TRUSTED
//    length: ft x 0.3048 = 0.3048 m; angle: degrees x 57.29577951308232 (= DEG_TO_RAD) per radian.
//    aid.handbook_pass._per_rad / _per_deg were NOT used: they are heuristic
//    (`if a > 1: convert else pass`), _per_rad is a no-op below 1.0, and on this
//    aircraft that silently makes a DATCOM rate derivative 57x too small.  Every
//    per-degree number here is multiplied by 57.29577951308232 explicitly.
//    Every array in this file is per radian and every length is SI.
//    cx[0] -- Cd0 in Tornado's own build-up -- = -0.017219.
//    Source of it: source WG.CD0 (the VLM has no profile drag: CD(0) - K*CL(0)^2 = -0.001673).
//    CD(0) = 0.000603563 and K*CL(0)^2 = 0.00227614 with K = 0.0803732,
//    so CD(0) - K*CL(0)^2 is negative: a linear vortex-lattice run has no profile
//    drag at all.  The source file's own WG.CD0 = 0.017219 is used instead.
//
// 5. THE MOMENT REFERENCE SHIFT
//    Tornado reports about geo['ref_point'] = [0, 0, 0] while geo['CG'] = [2.94, 0, 0] ft, so the
//    reference point is 2.94 ft AHEAD of the CG.  Tornado's x axis is AFT-positive, so the offset
//    handed to shift_moments_to_cg is dx = -ft(2.94) = -0.896112 m (NOT +), with dy = dz = 0.
//    Tornado's lift is up-positive while plane/dynamics.py's cz is the body +z force with z DOWN,
//    so every vertical-force argument is cz = -CL.  Slopes shift with slopes (Cm_a with -CL_a,
//    Cm_Q with -CL_Q, Cm_de with -CL_de) and the Cm0 intercept shifts with the -CL(0) intercept;
//    the yaw slopes shift with the side force (Cn_beta with CY_b, Cn_p with CY_P, Cn_r with CY_R).
//
// 6. SIGN CONVENTION
//    Tornado's axes are x aft, y right, z up; plane/dynamics.py's are x forward, y right, z down.
//    So cz = -CL, cl = -Cl, cm = +Cm, cn = -Cn.  The rate derivatives need NO extra flip: the
//    code perturbs the relative wind with r x omega, which is the correct omega x r once the
//    velocity is negated.  Signs are then normalised mechanically against aero_convert.units.SIGN_INVARIANTS
//    (data/planes/linear/morelli.json is the convention authority) and every flip is logged in
//    provenance.flipped.  cm0 carries no invariant and is recorded as not-normalised.
//    data/planes/linear/morelli.json's cz[1] sign is treated as that file's defect: the load-bearing
//    identity is cz = -CL, so a stable aircraft has cz[1] < 0 and cm[1] < 0.
//
// 7. PER-SLOT PROVENANCE (all 19 arrays; real solver output vs zeroed)
//   cz[1]     cl_alpha   normalised     tornado CL_a = -5.14801 -> -5.14801
//   cz[0]     cl0        normalised     tornado CL(alpha=0) = -0.168285 -> -0.168285
//   czq[0]    cl_q       normalised     tornado CL_Q = -9.59113 -> -9.59113
//   cy[0]     cy_beta    normalised     tornado CY_b = -0.40827 -> -0.40827
//   cyp[0]    cy_p       flipped        tornado CY_P = 0.159618 -> -0.159618
//   cyr[0]    cy_r       flipped        tornado CY_R = -0.386951 -> 0.386951
//   cl[0]     cl_beta    normalised     tornado Cl_b = -0.0537212 -> -0.0537212
//   clp[0]    cl_p       flipped        tornado Cl_P = 0.486095 -> -0.486095
//   clr[0]    cl_r       flipped        tornado Cl_R = -0.044525 -> 0.044525
//   cm[1]     cm_alpha   normalised     tornado Cm_a = -1.21856 -> -1.21856
//   cm[0]     cm0        not-normalised tornado Cm(alpha=0) = 0.0154461 -> 0.0154461
//   cmq[0]    cm_q       normalised     tornado Cm_Q = -19.2498 -> -19.2498
//   cn[0]     cn_beta    normalised     tornado Cn_b = 0.146473 -> 0.146473
//   cnp[0]    cn_p       normalised     tornado Cn_P = -0.0295649 -> -0.0295649
//   cnr[0]    cn_r       flipped        tornado Cn_R = 0.1916 -> -0.1916
//   cxq[0]    cd_q       normalised     tornado CX_Q = 0.00707928 -> 0.00707928
//   cx[0]     cd0        normalised     tornado CD at alpha = 0 = -0.017219 -> -0.017219
//   clda[0]   cl_da      normalised     tornado tornado_controls[aileron].Cl = -0.245288 -> -0.245288
//   cy[1]     cy_da      flipped        tornado tornado_controls[aileron].CY (= CC) = -0.0501724 -> 0.0501724
//   cnda[0]   cn_da      flipped        tornado tornado_controls[aileron].Cn = 0.017841 -> -0.017841
//   cldr[0]   cl_dr      flipped        tornado tornado_controls[rudder].Cl = -0.0214546 -> 0.0214546
//   cy[2]     cy_dr      flipped        tornado tornado_controls[rudder].CY (= CC) = -0.229426 -> 0.229426
//   cndr[0]   cn_dr      flipped        tornado tornado_controls[rudder].Cn = 0.183276 -> -0.183276
//   cz[5]     cl_de      normalised     tornado tornado_controls[elevator].CL = -0.371259 -> -0.371259
//   cm[2]     cm_de      normalised     tornado tornado_controls[elevator].Cm = -1.16212 -> -1.16212
//   every slot in plane.groups.nonlinear_index is exactly 0.0; CD_alpha is not
//   representable in this schema (cx has no CD*alpha term) and is zeroed and declared
//
// 8. HOW TO REGENERATE THIS FILE
//    cd python && python3 scripts/build_cessna172_aero.py
//    Nothing else writes these files; the sibling analysis and the sibling aid tree
//    are read-only inputs and all solver scratch goes to a temporary directory.
// ==========================================================================
